---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { profile } from "../data/profile";
---

<Layout title="Accessibility | Songyang Liu">
  <div class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Using this website</p><h1>Accessibility</h1><p>
      This personal website is designed with WCAG 2.1 Level A and AA
      requirements in mind. Accessibility is an ongoing effort; automated checks
      do not constitute a complete compliance certification.
    </p>
  </div>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="navigation">
    <h2 id="navigation">Navigation & reading</h2><p>
      A skip link leads to the main content. Links and figure descriptions can
      be operated with a keyboard, and focused controls have a visible outline.
      The layout adapts to narrow screens and increased text spacing. Research
      images include alternative text and expandable descriptions.
    </p><p>
      The academic CV is provided as an HTML web edition. The homepage and CV
      contain still images. The two locally hosted project pages also include
      short, silent video excerpts with native controls.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="section" id="project-media" aria-labelledby="project-media-heading">
    <h2 id="project-media-heading">Project videos & source materials</h2>
    <p>Building Immunology and Surgery AI are adapted from DreamXLab’s public project repository. Each image has alternative text and a longer explanation. Each video has a complete HTML description, a timed WebVTT description track, and source attribution. Figures can be opened at their original resolution. Research diagrams retain their original colors; labels and text explain their meaning independently of color.</p>
    <p>Silent videos can start when visible and pause outside the viewport or in a hidden tab. Native controls support manual playback and pause; manual pause is remembered. Reduced-motion and data-saving preferences disable automatic playback. Keyboard users can Tab to a video and use Space to play or pause it. Native controls also remain available without JavaScript.</p>
    <p>The web excerpts retain complete frames and original motion speed. The Building Immunology source has no audio. The surgical concept animations have digitally silent audio tracks. Laboratory sounds are omitted from the benchtop excerpt, which is presented as a silent visual demonstration. Original media remain unchanged in the source repository.</p>
    <p>These pages distinguish project goals, hardware illustrations, and demonstration footage from evidence in cited publications. Building Immunology’s bibliography retains the original authors; it is not presented as Songyang Liu’s personal publication list. Full screen-reader usability and external PDF reading order have not been certified.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="attachments">
    <h2 id="attachments">Research papers & external websites</h2><p>
      Paper links open publisher or repository pages that may offer HTML and PDF
      versions. Project pages are linked separately. Their content and
      accessibility can differ from this website. PDF tagging, reading order,
      equations, and screen-reader compatibility have not been fully verified
      for external publications.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="checks">
    <h2 id="checks">Testing</h2><p>
      Release checks include axe scans targeting WCAG 2.1 A and AA, keyboard
      navigation, 320 CSS-pixel reflow, increased text spacing, image
      descriptions, and heading structure. Manual review remains necessary,
      including evaluation with assistive technology.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="help">
    <h2 id="help">Report an accessibility issue</h2><p>
      If a page, figure, or linked publication is difficult to access, email <a
        href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a
      > with the page address and the information you need. Please include your browser
      or assistive technology if relevant.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
